<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tetrarchy</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">293 CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century">3rd century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Tetrarchy was the system of imperial government established by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diocletian">Diocletian</a> in 293 CE, under which the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a> was ruled by four emperors: two senior Augusti and two junior Caesars. Each was responsible for a different region, allowing closer defence of the frontiers. The Tetrarchy and Constantine's reforms temporarily stabilised the empire after the crisis of the third century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tetrarchy.jpg" alt="Tetrarchy" width="280" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nino Barbieri (talk · contribs) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Venice_%E2%80%93_The_Tetrarchs_03.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
